Assumptions
Product and Pricing Data is rationalized and is ready before Salesforce Opportunity Management changes and CPQ project is kicked off
Business Process changes are reviewed and approved with the right stakeholders before CPQ Project is kicked off
Customizations will be reviewed and approved by Zuora Leadership & Product Team
Billing and Revenue team will analyze downstream impacts from CPQ Implementation
CLM vendor is finalized to automate and integrate with CPQ proposal, templates and redlining process
Need confirmation from Zuora CPQ Product team for 3 user stories that are in roadmap
Use Case#1 - Availability of rules that enables guided configurations
Use Case#2 - ABP functionality within CPQx (currently ABP is enabled only in Zuora Billing)
Use Case#3 - Rule that will enable Guided Selling to the users

Zuora stakeholders will review and approve user stories associated with Epics that need Customization;  this is a tentative list and these stories will be reviewed with business during Grooming sessions 
Ability for the sales user to compare Zuora Products - feature is Compare Products 
Ability for the sales user to create Quote revisions (this is different from creating multiple Quotes per opportunity)
Ability for the sales user to perform bulk actions on Quote cart page
Ability for the sales users to request additional users to edit quotes using Quote Collaboration
Ability for the system to auto create Renewal Opportunities and Quote automatically based on subscription end date 

