Salesforce and Data Integrity Challenges
Issues with database cleanup, outdated BUs, post-acquisition data tracking, maintaining Zuora and SFDC parity, inconsistent data in SFDC, accessibility issues.
Challenges with contact data assignment, turnover affecting data quality, tracking new hires, adding new contacts.
Salesforce data trust issues, data cleanup, compliance with usage limits.
Reduced data reliability, leading to ineffective strategies and processes.
Manual updates needed for Salesforce data inaccuracies and subscription changes.

Inadequate Integration and Data Sources - Data sources scattered across systems, including billing systems and Microsoft, affecting data accuracy.
Identifying Gaps in Processes and Systems - Challenges in addressing gaps in processes and systems, especially concerning master data.

Strategic and Operational Challenges
Limited traction, heavy workload in strategy planning.
Compliance handling, renewal notification challenges, digital 'detective walls', collaboration with CSMs and Engineers.
Sales efficiency and data management issues.
Excessive reliance on manual renewal processes, complexity in managing various renewal scenarios like flat renewals, uplifts, and partial turns.
Frequent Changes and Lack of Centralized Information - Confusion due to frequent procedural changes.
Lack of Visibility and Involvement from the Deals Desk - Concerns about the Deals Desk not being sufficiently involved in sales and compensation activities.
Opportunity Management and Cross-Product Compatibility
Difficulties with cloning opportunities, non-interchangeable opportunities across products.
Cumbersome opportunity management, transition in sales team structure, quoting process challenges.
Difficulty in managing multiple subscriptions and renewal opportunities under one account, particularly with add-ons or changes, lack of automation in updating opportunities
Product Catalog Complexity - Difficulties with new or end-of-life products.
 Manual Creation of Ramp Opportunities - The deal desk team manually creating ramp opportunities, Challenges in creating opportunities for forecasting and managing configurations
Complexity in Opportunity Management - Difficulties in managing configurations and lead generation from marketing.
Quoting, Deal Desk Coordination,-  and Compliance
Complexities with non-standard proposals, offline work with CPQ, dependency on deal desk.
Lack of Recent Quoting, Tends to bypass the quoting step, focus instead on delivering value.
Managing quotes with different products, visibility into approval status, dependency on tools for opportunity management.
Reliance on deal desk for generating PDF quotes.

 Quote Expiration Issues, Manual creation of elements for renewals adds complexity, The renewal process is heavily manual, Increased workload, Managing add-ons and amendments requires creating new orders and bookings
Manual Quote Creation and Management, Limited Visibility System Automation for Approvals - Manual approval processes causing inefficiencies, Difficulties with new or end-of-life products.
Challenges in Pricing and Discounting - Difficulties with contractual discounts and bundling pricing.
Manual Interventions in Quote Creation - Manual edits required during the conversion of opportunities to quotes, Inconsistencies in the automation of approval processes., Confusion caused by the multitude of products and pricing structures.
Order-Quote Discrepancies
Encounters issues with order-quote discrepancies, depends on Clari for opportunity management, and has difficulty finding provisioning data.
Struggles with reviewing past order forms in Salesforce and determining historical pricing and discounts.
Faces limitations in self-service proposal generation, relying on the Deal Desk for PDF quotes even for standard approvals.
Misalignment and manual reconciliation efforts between renewal orders and quotes.
Discrepancies Between Quoted Products and Billing System - Mismatches between quoted products and IQ system availability.
Issues with Updating Billing Fields - Challenges in maintaining accurate billing information.
Financial Modeling and Post-Order Processing
No tool for complex financial modeling, manual checking on consumption vs. revenue, order-quote discrepancies.
Limited Progress in Gaining Traction, Lack of data for informed decision-making
Managing non-standard terms like opt-outs and price holds manually.
Challenges in Approval Updates due to Sales Hierarchy Changes, Challenges in maintaining accurate billing information, Payment Terms and Discounting - Need for clarity in managing payment terms and discounts.
 Issues with currency conversion affecting customer satisfaction.
Renewal Process Optimization
 Manual, time-consuming quote building and management, lacking auto-update and cloning features, with limited visibility into pricing and discounts.
Challenges in the Renewal Process - Inefficiencies when dealing with large customers during renewals.
Contract Renewal and Upsell/Downsell - Ambiguity around managing renewals and contract changes.
