Attributes & Options
Attributes
Selection that impacts the features or pricing of a product.
Improves the User experience to a great extent. 
Captures information related to the Product being configured
Helps in reducing the SKU proliferation
Typically a field that holds the information related to the product being configured.
Eg: Selecting the edition (Professional, Enterprise..) of Sales-Cloud would automatically provide the eligible features instead of each selecting each feature independently 
Options
Typically a product record that gets selected within the context of Bundle. This gets added as a separate line item
Can have it’s own price and independent attributes
Can be fulfilled independently
Eg: Add-On Storage space from Salesforce can be an Option as the storage can be procured at a later stage independent from Sales-Cloud licenses
94

Building Offers
Subscription Model primarily moves away from Individual Product based Pricing to a Offer based Pricing. The Offer may contain
Hardware ( OnPrem/Cloud)
Software
Upgrades

Bundles/Offers need to be created to cater the solution in its entirety rather than asking the customer/sales rep to pick from a set of products in a catalog.

Predefined offers based on your best selling items.
Technical Services
Installation
Managed Services
95

Products & Configurations - Guidelines
Build Models using Product Structures (bundles) & Rules rather than sku based models - Balance usability vs maintenance
Define the Category Hierarchy to navigate and find the products easily (No more than 3 levels)
Enable Recommendations - for Upsells and Cross-sells & Replacements
Leverage Out of the Box setup and avoid customizations in the Product Setup.
Avoid offline Tools (ex: excel) & Processes (Email Approvals)
Add Favorites based on Common Solutions/Market Segments for reusability
Define Proper Product Name/Code/Description/ Image and other Product Metadata for a good user experience in the tool


