Billing Guidelines
Generate Billing Schedules and initiate Invoice creation once an Order is fulfilled 
Assets should be created, activated, and stored against a customer record upon order fulfillment
Optimize the handoffs and collaboration between Operations and Billing - Enable Orders to seamlessly flow into Billing with minimal user intervention
Structure the Sales Account hierarchy to accommodate how customers are billed – Look at how “Bill To’s”, “Ship To’s” should be leveraged to ensure the correct customers are billed and invoiced
Leverage standard capabilities from currently used systems like Salesforce Feed Tracking and historical Billing reporting to track how billing has been modified over time
Use automated notifications and reporting to alert key stakeholders (Sales, Ops, etc.) to important customer or billing related milestones in order to proactively serve the customer 
Enable appropriate integrations with Tax and Payment systems to complete the automated payment process for credit card payments.


